name,model,A,B,g,tis_cap,reference,notes
polished_fused_silica,abg,3e-5,1e-4,2,,"ABg scatter model form: Pfisterer, 'Approximated Scatter Models for Stray Light Analysis,' Optics & Photonics News (2011); low-scatter mirror-grade fused-silica surface, representative super-polished fit (TIS ~ 0.09% near normal), cf. Harvey et al., 'Total integrated scatter from surfaces with arbitrary roughness,' Opt. Eng. 51, 013402 (2012).","UNVERIFIED — A/B/g are representative of a super-polished fused-silica surface, not transcribed from a specific published fit; check against a measured BSDF before production use. g=2 => closed-form radial CDF."
polished_bk7_glass,abg,1e-3,1e-3,2,,"ABg model (Pfisterer, Optics & Photonics News 2011); standard commercially-polished N-BK7 glass surface (60-40 scratch-dig class), representative fit (TIS ~ 2.2% near normal).","UNVERIFIED — representative values for a conventionally polished glass surface, not a specific vendor datasheet; verify before production use. g=2."
diamond_turned_aluminum,abg,8e-3,1e-2,2,0.1,"ABg model (Pfisterer, Optics & Photonics News 2011); single-point diamond-turned aluminum mirror, elevated scatter from periodic turning marks, representative fit (raw TIS ~ 11.6%, capped at measured 10%). Compare Harvey-Shack treatment of turned metals, Opt. Eng. 51, 013402 (2012).","UNVERIFIED — representative of a diamond-turned metal mirror; tis_cap=0.1 pins the split to a plausible measured total scatter. Actual turned surfaces are anisotropic (grooved); this isotropic ABg fit is an approximation. g=2."
